roduced with federal funds.  aIn scope of the U.S. Government Publishing Office Cataloging and Indexing Program (C&I) and Federal Depository Library Program (FDLP).  aThis assessment report identifies the major post-Staggers impediments to the grain marketing and transportation system and recommends actions to alleviate these problems. the Office of Transportation visited 48 grain shippers in the summer of 1983 and conducted nine regional workshops in 1983-84.2 aExecutive summary and recommendations -- Assessment update (Adequacy of information on rail contracts ; Educational and technical assistance in rate negotiations ; Market dominance as it applies in rate reasonableness proceedings ; Joint rates, through rates, and reciprocal switchings ; Other concerns) -- Appendices.10aUnited States.tStaggers Rail Act of 1980. 0aGrain tradezUnited States.07aStaggers Rail Act of 1980 (United States)2fast0(OCoLC)fst01365615 7aGrain trade.2fast0(OCoLC)fst00946068 7aUnited States.2fast0(OCoLC)fst012041551https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJtxgQXMWqmjMjjwXRHgrq 7aContract rates.2trt 7aFreight transportation.2trt 7aRailroads.2trt1 aUnited States.bDepartment of Agriculture.bOffice of Transportation.08iOnline version:tEffects of the Staggers Rail Act on grain marketing.w(OCoLC)624415986  aC0bGPO  aVEND01b20260529  aHistoric Shelflist Drawer 68; HSL002; 2026092103015cam a2200613 a 00020583920260918134124.0841219s1984    dcubk    s   f000 0 eng d  a12257822699 agp^85008055  a(OCoLC)11510968z(OCoLC)1225782269  a003-024-05105-2bGPO  aGPObengcGPOdOCLdOCLCQdTXJdOCLCQdOCLCFdOCLCQdOCLCOdXFFdOCLCOdOCLdOCLCAdUMKdOCLCOdOCLCQdOCLCOdGPOdOCLCOdOCLCLdOCLCQdGPO  an-us-tx  aGPOO 4aHA657b.T49 1980  a0159-C-430 aC 3.223/20:80-4-45/2  aPHC 80-4-450 aCensus of population and housing (1980)10a1980 census of population and housing.pCongressional districts of the 99th Congress.nPart 45.pTexas.